Conditional Workflows in GitHub Actions

Today I learned how conditions control whether jobs or steps run based on specific rules.

🔹 if Conditions
if conditions allow workflows to:
Run only when conditions match
Skip unnecessary execution
Handle different scenarios
They add logic to CI/CD.

🔹 Job-Level Conditions
Job-level if:
Controls whether a job runs
Evaluated before job starts
Useful for environment-specific jobs

🔹 Step-Level Conditions
Step-level if:
Controls individual steps
Allows fine-grained execution
Useful for optional tasks

🔥 3-Line Takeaway
Conditions add logic.
 Jobs control stages.
 Steps control actions.
